        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177507094?u=02fca01b2bde41566660e171c995c01443421086&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Include a note on the importance of setting <code class=\"notranslate\">width</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">height</code> for effective <code class=\"notranslate\">object-fit</code> application.</p>\n\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">I added a note about how to use the <code class=\"notranslate\">object-fit</code> property effectively</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Because I lost a lot of time trying to understand why the <code class=\"notranslate\">object-fit</code> property doesn't work on my personal examples, I did what the docs instruct, but that property fails to apply. And just later I discovered that I should set a <strong>height</strong> and <strong>width</strong> to the image in order for that <code class=\"notranslate\">object-fit</code> to be applied effectively. I think that works the same for all the replaced-elements, but I only tested it for <code class=\"notranslate\">img</code> elements.</li>\n<li>Readers will be able to use that <code class=\"notranslate\">object-fit</code> effectively.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">There is no clue or note about that even in the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/object-fit\" rel=\"nofollow\">object-fit mdn-reference</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
