        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44868357?u=096bd31a657e3fc94f4821b3b53e251c7c1d07f6&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This updates the explanation of how <code class=\"notranslate\">attr()</code> behaves when used in URL-related contexts.<br>\nThe previous text implied a general restriction, but the real limitation applies <strong>only when the value is required to be a <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;url&gt;</code> type</strong>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The revised wording explains that:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">attr()</code> values are <em>attr-tainted</em>.</li>\n<li>Using them in a context requiring a <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;url&gt;</code> (e.g. inside <code class=\"notranslate\">url()</code> or <code class=\"notranslate\">background-image</code>) results in IACVT.</li>\n<li>Some functions—such as <code class=\"notranslate\">image-set()</code>—accept a <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;string&gt;</code> first, which is later interpreted as a URL. This can allow <code class=\"notranslate\">attr()</code> to work <strong>in shorthand properties like <code class=\"notranslate\">background</code></strong>, although <strong>it does not work in <code class=\"notranslate\">background-image</code></strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This update was made after watching a video by <a href=\"https://space.bilibili.com/31556431\" rel=\"nofollow\">zhangxinxu</a> on bilibili:<br>\n<a href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1dPkzB3Esx\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1dPkzB3Esx</a><br>\nI realized the documentation should more accurately reflect the difference between <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;url&gt;</code>-required contexts and cases where <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;string&gt;</code> is allowed before URL resolution.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41948",
            "title": "Clarify `attr()` URL limitations and add `image-set()` example",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-20T00:29:15.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-14T09:43:46.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "codersjj",
                "url": "https://github.com/codersjj"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">As discussed in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3623204721\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41938\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/41938/hovercard?comment_id=3530152718&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41938#issuecomment-3530152718\">#41938 (comment)</a> , response headers should not have the section on \"forbidden request headers\". I have modified this so that response headers listed in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3623204721\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41938\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/41938/hovercard?comment_id=3530227774&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41938#issuecomment-3530227774\">#41938 (comment)</a> now have \"Forbidden response header\" instead.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I also updated the request and response headers to include the forbidden response information.</p>",
